      "title": "Testing Node.js: Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Testing Node.js: Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Runner and assertions",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`describe`/`it`/`test` ==register== tests; the **runner** runs them",
                "A ==thrown error== marks the test failed",
                "Runner: finds, runs, reports. `assert`/`expect`: only ==throw== on mismatch"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Arrange-Act-Assert",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Set up inputs, call the unit ==once==, assert the outcome",
                "==One behavior== per test"
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "import { test } from 'node:test';",
                "import assert from 'node:assert/strict';",
                "test('adds tax', () => {",
                "  const price = 100;           // arrange",
                "  const total = addTax(price); // act",
                "  assert.equal(total, 120);    // assert",
                "});"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Unit vs integration",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Unit",
                "Integration"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Scope",
                  "One module",
                  "Real pieces wired"
                ],
                [
                  "Deps",
                  "Test doubles",
                  "Real or in-memory DB"
                ],
                [
                  "Example",
                  "Service + fake repo",
                  "HTTP layer + DB"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Test behavior",
              "text": "Assert **public output**, not private calls. Internal assertions ==break on every refactor==."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Runner vs assert?** Runner executes; assert throws.",
                "**Unit vs integration?** Doubles vs real pieces.",
                "**Why not assert internals?** Refactors break tests."
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "node:test and assert",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "node:test and assert",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Built In, No Install",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`import { test, describe, it, before, after, beforeEach, afterEach } from 'node:test'`",
                "Run with ==node --test==: finds `*.test.js` and files under `test/`",
                "Async test functions are ==awaited automatically=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Flag",
                "Does"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`--watch`",
                  "re-run on file change"
                ],
                [
                  "`--test-name-pattern='login'`",
                  "only matching names"
                ],
                [
                  "`--experimental-test-coverage`",
                  "coverage report"
                ],
                [
                  "`--test-reporter=spec`",
                  "readable output"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Assertions",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Import `node:assert/strict`: `equal` is then ==`===`==, `deepEqual` is strict deep equality",
                "Loose non-strict `assert.equal` uses `==`",
                "`assert.throws(fn, /msg/)` for **sync** errors",
                "`await assert.rejects(promise, { name: 'TypeError' })` for **async** errors"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Forgot await?",
              "text": "Without `await`, `assert.rejects` is never checked and the test ==passes falsely==."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Spies and Fake Time",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`t.mock.fn()` and `t.mock.method(obj, 'name')` make spies",
                "They ==auto-restore== after the test"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "t.mock.timers.enable({ apis: ['setTimeout'] });",
                "setTimeout(cb, 1000);",
                "t.mock.timers.tick(1000); // cb fires now"
              ],
              "note": "fakes time, no real waiting"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Jest vs Vitest",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Jest vs Vitest",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Same API, different engine",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Both ship ==describe/it/expect==, matchers, mocks, snapshots, coverage",
                "{blue:Vitest}: Vite-powered, native ESM + TypeScript, fast watch",
                "{orange:Jest}: needs a transform (==babel== or ==ts-jest==) for ESM/TS",
                "Jest globals are automatic: `jest.fn`, `jest.mock`",
                "Vitest needs `globals: true` in config, or an import",
                "Vitest mock namespace is ==vi==, not `jest`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "import { describe, it, expect, vi } from 'vitest'",
                "",
                "const send = vi.fn()"
              ],
              "note": "explicit imports when globals is off"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Matchers and async",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Matcher",
                "Checks"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`toBe`",
                  "`Object.is` identity"
                ],
                [
                  "`toEqual`",
                  "deep equality"
                ],
                [
                  "`toStrictEqual`",
                  "deep + `undefined` props + class types"
                ],
                [
                  "`toThrow`",
                  "call wrapped: `expect(() => fn()).toThrow()`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`await expect(p).resolves.toBe(1)`",
                "`await expect(p).rejects.toThrow('x')`",
                "Guard with `expect.assertions(n)`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Un-awaited expect",
              "text": "An expect without `await` ==never fails== the test. Await it, or guard with `expect.assertions(n)`."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Commands",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Jest",
                "Vitest"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Watch",
                  "`npx jest --watch`",
                  "`npx vitest` (default in terminal)"
                ],
                [
                  "Filter",
                  "`npx jest path -t 'name'`",
                  "`npx vitest path -t 'name'`"
                ],
                [
                  "CI one-shot",
                  "`npx jest`",
                  "`npx vitest run`"
                ]
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Mocking Modules and Timers",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Mocking Modules and Timers",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Doubles",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Double",
                "Job"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Spy",
                  "==observes== a real call"
                ],
                [
                  "Stub",
                  "replaces the return value"
                ],
                [
                  "Mock",
                  "adds call expectations"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`jest.fn()` / `vi.fn()` with `mockReturnValue`, `mockResolvedValue`, `mockImplementation`",
                "Assert with `toHaveBeenCalledWith`, `toHaveBeenCalledTimes`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Modules and Spies",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "jest.mock('./mailer', () => ({ send: jest.fn() }));",
                "import { send } from './mailer';",
                "send.mockResolvedValue(true);",
                "expect(send).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);"
              ],
              "note": "factory form"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`jest.mock` / `vi.mock` is ==hoisted== above imports",
                "Vitest factory returns the export shape, incl. `default`",
                "`spyOn(obj, 'm')` wraps a real method; `mockRestore` or `restoreMocks: true`",
                "`afterEach`: `clearAllMocks` wipes calls, `resetAllMocks` wipes implementations"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Timers and Gotchas",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Call",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`useFakeTimers()`",
                  "fake clock on"
                ],
                [
                  "`advanceTimersByTime(1000)`",
                  "fires due timers"
                ],
                [
                  "`runAllTimers()`",
                  "fires all pending"
                ],
                [
                  "`setSystemTime(date)`",
                  "sets `Date.now`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "ESM imports are static: mock first (`vi.hoisted`, Jest `unstable_mockModule`)",
                "Awaited promises need `advanceTimersByTimeAsync`",
                "Mocking too much means testing the mocks"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Clean up",
              "text": "Call ==useRealTimers()== in `afterEach`, or fake time leaks."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
